WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.013
- Come on, Todd.

00:00:02.013 --> 00:00:03.610
Pick up, pick up, pick
up, pick up, pick up.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:06.490
- Hey, I was wondering if
I'd hear from you Todd-ay.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.297
Yes-Todd-ay, I thought,

00:00:08.297 --> 00:00:11.170
"Maybe I'll hear from her Todd-morrow."

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.190
- Is Untitled Princess
Carolyn Project okay?

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.430
- She sure is!

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.263
- Oh, thank God.

00:00:15.263 --> 00:00:16.600
- [Todd] Wait, you're talking about

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.850
Untitled Princess Carolyn
Project the baby, right?

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.720
- Who else would I be talking about?

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.744
- Well...

00:00:22.744 --> 00:00:24.850
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.830
- Mr. Knickerbocker will see you now.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:27.663
- Great!

00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:28.496
(phone rings)

00:00:28.496 --> 00:00:30.030
Oh, hold on one second.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.863
Hello?

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.380
- Todd, I have to go to a photo shoot.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.360
I need you to take the
baby for an hour or so.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.710
- Well, you know how
much I love hanging out

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.110
with Untitled Princess Carolyn Project,

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:42.100
but I can't Todd-ay, because
of all these meetings I have,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.303
but if my schedule
weren't so busy, I'd say,

00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:48.550
"Sure, I'd be happy to."

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.300
- Great, I'll see you at
Vim in fifteen minutes.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.300
- Um, okay?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.263
I'll be right back.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:56.070
Sorry about that.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.340
(phones ring)

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.173
Hello?

00:00:59.173 --> 00:01:00.900
- Todd, change of plans,
bring the baby over to me

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.060
at Smash Fox Studios.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.360
- Okay, he had to cancel another meeting,

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.800
but he will see you now.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.850
- I'll be right back.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.480
- I'm going to level with you, Todd,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.400
you making me wait made me angry,

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.100
and that made me respect you.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.110
- Sorry, things have
just been a little hectic

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.120
since I've been helping out

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.300
with Untitled Princess Carolyn Project.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.570
- Untitled Princess Carolyn Project?

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:22.730
I'm intrigued.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.480
You think the project has legs?

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.970
- Yeah, she has legs.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.350
- I'm thrilled to meet you.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.170
The whole town is buzzing about

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.985
Untitled Princess Carolyn Project.

00:01:31.985 --> 00:01:33.810
- Weird, but okay.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.070
- We need something big.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.680
Is Untitled Princess Carolyn Project

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.540
the kind of thing that makes lot of noise?

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.620
- She sure does!

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.230
- I'm in, name your price.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:42.780
- Um...

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.920
Jonathan?

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.800
- We took a big swing with
Dick Wolf's Milwaukee shows.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.440
Turns out audiences are not interested

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.780
in a whole night of Milwaukee,

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.520
so now we've got some slots to fill.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.330
Do you think Untitled
Princess Carolyn Project

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.950
could live for several seasons?

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.110
- I don't see how those
things are related,

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.080
but I certainly hope so.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.500
- Well, how can I help?

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.360
- You wanna help?

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.720
- Let's start with a two season pick-up.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:05.553
- Yeah, sure!

00:02:05.553 --> 00:02:08.033
Pick-up, drop-off, whatever
works best for you.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.610
That would be great.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:10.443
- Great!

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.010
- Well, here she is.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.430
What time do you want me to pick her up?

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.210
- Wait, it's a baby?

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.093
- And she has legs.

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:21.450
- I already canceled
Milwaukee Waste Management.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.100
I told the shareholders this
was gonna save the network.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.910
We designed the poster!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.620
Todd, we need a show.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.263
We can't air a baby!

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:34.810
- So, long story short,
Pinky canceled the baby,

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.115
but now we owe him a TV show.

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:37.948
- Huh.

